00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.820
Should we talk a little
bit about what those are

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:52.360
and why those are important?

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:56.550
CYRIL TOVENA: A game
server is [INAUDIBLE]

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:58.320
in multiplayer video games.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:00.390
And the idea is it
actually receives

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:05.190
all the events of the player and
then you can do some game logic

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:07.680
and also send back the
information to all the players

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.900
so they can render the actual
[INAUDIBLE] on the console.

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:11.650
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:06:11.650 --> 00:06:14.520
So dedicated game servers are
really important for, I think,

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:15.754
two particular reasons--

00:06:15.754 --> 00:06:17.170
very fast-paced
multiplayer games,

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:18.810
so like your "Overwatches,"
and your "Fortnites,"

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:19.810
and those kind of games.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.330
One of which is,
unfortunately, we

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:22.500
can't change the speed of light.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.000
It would be really
nice if we could.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.670
So being able to control the
physical location of where

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:29.080
all your players connect
to is really powerful.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:30.600
So if we're playing a
game-- we're here at Next--

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.100
if we could put a server
that was actually in

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:33.690
[INAUDIBLE] that would be
great, because it's actually

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:34.560
close to us.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.260
Ideally, we wouldn't want to
build a server in Australia.

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:38.380
That would be sad.

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:40.020
And the other fun
thing is, I don't

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:43.060
know if you've actually noticed
this, but people are horrible.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:44.019
So-- [LAUGHS]

00:06:44.019 --> 00:06:45.810
MELANIE WARWICK: Well,
that's a revelation.

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:47.610
FRANCESC CAMPOY: I did work
with you for quite a long time.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:48.720
MARK MANDEL: I know,
so that's true.

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.053
And so you've definitely notice.

00:06:50.053 --> 00:06:51.730
Melanie is still
working this out.

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:54.360
And so any time you give a
binary to someone or people

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.720
can see the traffic that
happens between systems,

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:59.070
they're going to introspect
it and try and cheat things.

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:00.690
Basically, if you have
a dedicated game server,

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:01.980
you can make it authoritative.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:05.850
And it's one way of
helping with cheating.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.110
Anything you want to--

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:08.850
CYRIL TOVENA: No, I think you
also talk about the latency.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:11.190
I think this is something
that is very important.

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:15.649
When you have a game like a
FPS game, and a shooting game,

00:07:15.649 --> 00:07:17.440
it's very important to
have a good latency.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:20.451
So that's when you want to start
using dedicated game server.

