00:18:18.775 --> 00:18:20.294
[LAUGHTER]

00:18:20.294 --> 00:18:21.460
CYRIL TOVENA: Go, obviously.

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:22.835
FRANCESC CAMPOY:
Oh, interesting.

00:18:22.835 --> 00:18:23.898
[LAUGHTER]

00:18:23.898 --> 00:18:26.684
MELANIE WARWICK: Do you have any
specific questions around that?

00:18:26.684 --> 00:18:27.850
FRANCESC CAMPOY: I mean, no.

00:18:27.850 --> 00:18:29.710
Like I was going to
ask why you chose it,

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:31.530
but you're extending
Kubernetes, so I

00:18:31.530 --> 00:18:33.930
guess it's the way to do it.

00:18:33.930 --> 00:18:36.720
But actually, the question
would be the other way around.

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:38.460
Is there any
complaints about Go?

00:18:38.460 --> 00:18:40.270
Like, anything that
you face that's like,

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:42.184
oh, I wish I was doing closure.

00:18:42.184 --> 00:18:43.350
MARK MANDEL: It's the worst.

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:44.400
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Just the worst.

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:45.350
MARK MANDEL: It's
just the worst.

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:46.210
It's just I hate it.

00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:47.144
It's just the worse.

00:18:47.144 --> 00:18:48.560
MELANIE WARWICK:
All the problems.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:49.280
MARK MANDEL: No.

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:50.790
I mean, I personally like Go.

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:52.380
It's good for
getting stuff done.

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:54.090
Been using [INAUDIBLE]
as dependency management.

00:18:54.090 --> 00:18:54.880
It's fine.

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:55.590
It works.

00:18:55.590 --> 00:18:56.370
We haven't moved Vigo yet.

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:56.760
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Oh cool.

00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:57.520
MARK MANDEL: I don't know
what's happening there.

00:18:57.520 --> 00:18:58.110
MELANIE WARWICK: Well,
is there anything

00:18:58.110 --> 00:19:01.060
you would do differently if you
were to do this all over again?

00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:02.640
MARK MANDEL: I don't think so.

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:06.266
We go back and fix things if we
have decided it doesn't work.

00:19:06.266 --> 00:19:07.890
Like an example of
that that's actually

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:11.250
coming in this release is
initially we were like, oh,

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:11.890
games servers--

00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:13.110
or maybe I initially said it.

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:13.830
I don't know if it's a we.

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:15.120
It may have been a me thing.

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:16.530
Game servers only need one port.

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:17.750
And I was like, oh,
it will be fine.

00:19:17.750 --> 00:19:20.291
And then everyone was like, no,
they need more than one port.

00:19:20.291 --> 00:19:22.000
And I was like, OK,
let's change that.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:23.890
So that's coming in
this version now.

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:25.920
It's actually some half decent
backward compatibility too,

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:26.836
so that's all working.

00:19:26.836 --> 00:19:29.253
So we're pretty iterative,
especially being alpha as well.

00:19:29.253 --> 00:19:31.377
FRANCESC CAMPOY: What are
