00:19:56.056 --> 00:19:58.569
So we want to do some
statistics around players,

00:19:58.569 --> 00:20:00.360
like number of game
servers, visualizations

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:01.360
that kind of stuff.

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:03.720
But I think also do some
very standard metrics

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.855
for game servers, FPS
counts, lost frame

00:20:05.855 --> 00:20:07.730
counts, and hitching,
and that kind of stuff.

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:12.617
Multicluster is top
of mind as well.

00:20:12.617 --> 00:20:13.950
What else did I have on my list?

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:15.540
CYRIL TOVENA: Not auto scaling?

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:16.300
MARK MANDEL: Auto scaling.

00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:16.530
Yes.

00:20:16.530 --> 00:20:17.550
Yeah, that's another
thing that we

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:18.758
want to explore more as well.

00:20:18.758 --> 00:20:22.150
CYRIL TOVENA: Maybe Windows,
if it gets more [INAUDIBLE]..

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:22.650
Yeah.

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:23.650
MARK MANDEL: Yeah,
so Microsoft's

00:20:23.650 --> 00:20:25.470
been doing some pretty
amazing work with Windows

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:27.840
in Kubernetes, so we definitely
want to take advantage of that.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:30.540
Windows is pretty huge in the
games industry for some reason.

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:31.133
CYRIL TOVENA: Yeah, it is.

00:20:31.133 --> 00:20:31.920
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:34.630
FRANCESC CAMPOY: For
the server side too, or?

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:35.380
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:36.500
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Oh wow.

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.000
Interesting.

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:38.640
CYRIL TOVENA: Yeah, because
it's easier for the developers

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:40.320
when they're working on Windows.

00:20:40.320 --> 00:20:41.760
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Makes sense.

00:20:41.760 --> 00:20:43.140
MELANIE WARWICK: You talked
