involved anything else you

00:20:45.264 --> 00:20:48.270
wanted to say in regards to how,
if anybody wants to be involved

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:49.377
in building out Agones?

00:20:49.377 --> 00:20:50.710
Anything else you want to share?

00:20:50.710 --> 00:20:51.040
MARK MANDEL: Aboslutely.

00:20:51.040 --> 00:20:51.360
Yeah.

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:52.770
So there is a
contributing guide.

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:54.437
It's definitely the
best place to start.

00:20:54.437 --> 00:20:56.978
There's like a how to contribute
with a contributer's license

00:20:56.978 --> 00:20:59.130
agreement, code of conduct,
that kind of stuff,

00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:00.549
as well as a set of resources.

00:21:00.549 --> 00:21:02.340
There's a developing,
testing, and building

00:21:02.340 --> 00:21:04.500
Agones step-by-step
instruction guide

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:06.520
for basically getting
up and running.

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:08.190
We've got a whole
set of internal tools

00:21:08.190 --> 00:21:11.240
that we use for making builds
and running tests and doing

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:12.250
all that kind of stuff.

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:14.380
So that is literally the
first place to start.

00:21:14.380 --> 00:21:17.170
And we have it covering both
Windows and Linux and Mac,

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:19.590
and both running that on
Google Kubernetes Engine

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:21.584
as well as running
locally on Minikube.

00:21:21.584 --> 00:21:23.500
So basically that is the
first place to start.

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:25.020
And if you have any issues,
that's the first thing.

00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:26.160
Because then if
you can run that,

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:27.326
then you can compile things.

00:21:27.326 --> 00:21:29.337
You can run tests, that
kind of stuff as well.

00:21:29.337 --> 00:21:30.420
But it's been pretty cool.

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:32.070
We've had fly by contributions.

00:21:32.070 --> 00:21:34.470
Recently we had someone
come by and was like--

00:21:34.470 --> 00:21:37.416
so we have an integrated SDK
for lifecycle management.

00:21:37.416 --> 00:21:39.040
