here's one for us.

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:39.980
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Oh yeah, nice.

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.355
MARK MANDEL: Here you go.

00:21:41.355 --> 00:21:42.274
And we're like, cool.

00:21:42.274 --> 00:21:43.690
FRANCESC CAMPOY:
That's very nice.

00:21:43.690 --> 00:21:44.790
MARK MANDEL: Which
is really neat.

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:47.081
FRANCESC CAMPOY: So what if
I don't want to contribute,

00:21:47.081 --> 00:21:48.360
but I want to use it.

00:21:48.360 --> 00:21:50.110
Are you ready for that?

00:21:50.110 --> 00:21:52.830
If anyone wants to
consider building a game

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:55.110
server using Agones,
is it a good moment,

00:21:55.110 --> 00:21:56.610
or should they wait?

00:21:56.610 --> 00:21:59.670
MARK MANDEL: I would say it
depends on what your plans are.

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:01.900
If you want to release
in the next six weeks,

00:22:01.900 --> 00:22:03.600
maybe you don't.

00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:05.460
If you want to release
sometime next year,

00:22:05.460 --> 00:22:07.440
I think it's definitely
worth having a look at,

00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:09.232
especially if you don't
want vendor lock in

00:22:09.232 --> 00:22:11.356
and you want to be able to
run your stuff anywhere.

00:22:11.356 --> 00:22:12.794
I think that's pretty accurate.

00:22:12.794 --> 00:22:14.460
And I think it's also
a good opportunity

00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:15.876
as well to be able
to be like, OK,

00:22:15.876 --> 00:22:17.580
we can help shape
what this looks like

00:22:17.580 --> 00:22:19.050
